# What this repository holds: the engine and its tools (triview, rungs, tools), the timeline data (data),
# the scenes of record, the small records the builds write and read, and the documents (docs).
# What stays on disk only: frames, scans, videos and test scenes. They are large and can be rendered again.

# Python, Blender and Windows leftovers
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.blend1
*.blend2
exposure_probe_*.png
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Assets (rung 3 on): the scans and asset packs as downloaded and what is made from them. Since 2026-11-21 they travel
# in git, at his word, so that the work can go on from another computer, by tools/bigfiles.py (what it carries is
# listed in bigfiles/carry.txt; the files themselves are named in the block at the end of this file).
# assets/licensed holds a scan that is free to use with credit but whose files may not be given on. Nothing in it is a
# git file as itself: it enters git only as encrypted parts under bigfiles/, and so do the scenes that pack its maps.
/assets/licensed/
# assets/open is free to publish: its small files are plain git files, its files over 45 MB go in plain parts.
# Left out there: copies of what the zip beside them already holds.
/assets/open/lpshead/unpacked/
# A file that `join` is still writing, and any key file that strays in here.
*.joining
*.key

# Scenes: only the scenes named here are kept. Every other scene is a test build.
# To keep a new scene of record, add a line for it below.
/scenes/*
!/scenes/rung2p_r14m48.blend
!/scenes/rung2p_r14m49.blend
!/scenes/rung2p_r14m50.blend
!/scenes/rung2p_r14m51.blend

# Renders: everything is left out except the small records (json, jsonl, npz)
# and the pictured findings of a rung's audit.
/renders/**
!/renders/**/
!/renders/**/*.json
!/renders/**/*.jsonl
!/renders/**/*.npz
!/renders/rung2p/audit_r14/**
# A broken link left in renders since rung 2j: named here so that git does not try to open it.
/renders/rung2j$d

